CLEAN UP THE EXISTING SAI SMART AI PROPERTY FINDER APPLICATION BY SEPARATING THE THREE USER ROLES CORRECTLY:

1. BUYER / PROPERTY SEEKER
2. AGENT / BROKER
3. BUILDER — THE PERSON OR COMPANY THAT CONSTRUCTS APARTMENT BUILDINGS AND SELLS THE APARTMENTS/UNITS

IMPORTANT:
The current design has role contamination. Some users can see dashboards and features that belong to other roles.

Fix the existing design architecture so that each role has its own separate experience.

Do not redesign the entire application.
Do not change the existing SAI branding, colors, typography, layout style, or visual design system unnecessarily.
Do not create a Super Admin dashboard in this task.
Do not add new unrelated features.

The primary goal is to separate the Buyer, Agent, and Builder experiences and remove features from the wrong role.

==================================================
1. BUYER / PROPERTY SEEKER
==================================================

The Buyer is a person searching for a property to buy or rent.

The Buyer can:

- Browse available properties
- Search for properties
- Use AI-powered natural-language property search
- Use voice search
- Apply filters
- View property details
- View property locations on a map
- Save or favorite properties
- Compare properties
- View personalized property recommendations
- Contact the owner, agent, or builder
- Send enquiries
- View messages and conversations
- View saved properties
- View search history
- Manage their own profile and preferences

The Buyer must NOT be able to:

- Create a property listing
- Generate a property listing
- Add a new property
- Manage property listings
- Manage apartment projects
- Manage towers or buildings
- Manage apartment units or inventory
- Manage clients as an Agent
- Access the Agent Dashboard
- Access the Builder Dashboard
- Access any platform administration features

The Buyer navigation should contain only Buyer-related features:

- Home
- AI Search
- Explore Properties
- Map
- Saved Properties
- Compare
- Messages / Enquiries
- Profile

Remove the following from the Buyer experience if they currently appear:

- Add Property
- Create Listing
- Generate Listing
- Manage Listings
- Add Project
- My Projects
- Units / Inventory
- Agent Dashboard
- Builder Dashboard
- Admin Dashboard

A Buyer should be able to VIEW and ENQUIRE about properties, but should not be able to CREATE or MANAGE property listings.

==================================================
2. AGENT / BROKER
==================================================

The Agent is a real-estate professional or broker who represents properties and helps buyers find and purchase or rent them.

The Agent can:

- Access an Agent Dashboard
- Create property listings
- Add individual property listings
- Edit their own listings
- Manage their own listings
- Upload property images
- Add property details
- Upload documents for verification
- Submit properties for verification
- View verification status
- Manage buyer enquiries
- Manage leads
- Manage their own clients
- Communicate with interested buyers
- View analytics for their own listings
- Manage their professional Agent profile

The Agent should manage only:

- Their own listings
- Listings assigned to them
- Their own leads
- Their own clients
- Their own performance analytics

The Agent must NOT be able to:

- Access the Builder Dashboard
- Create or manage apartment construction projects as a Builder
- Manage towers or buildings belonging to a Builder
- Manage apartment inventory belonging to a Builder
- Manage all users on the platform
- Manage all properties on the platform
- Access platform-wide administration features
- Access the Super Admin Control Panel

The Agent navigation should contain only:

- Agent Overview
- My Listings
- Add Property
- Leads & Enquiries
- Clients
- Analytics
- Verification Status
- Messages
- Agent Profile

IMPORTANT:
Use the term "My Listings" for properties managed by the Agent.

Do not show the Agent all properties on the SAI platform as if the Agent manages the entire property database.

==================================================
3. BUILDER
==================================================

The Builder is the person or company that constructs apartment buildings or residential housing projects and sells the apartments or units within those projects.

The Builder is NOT a Buyer.

The Builder is NOT an Agent.

The Builder is responsible for their own constructed apartment projects.

For example:

A Builder creates:

GREEN VALLEY APARTMENTS
        ↓
    TOWER A
        ↓
    APARTMENT UNITS
        ↓
    Flat 101
    Flat 102
    Flat 103

The Builder can:

- Access a Builder Dashboard
- Create their own apartment project
- Add apartment project details
- Add project images
- Add project descriptions
- Add towers or buildings
- Add apartments or units
- Manage available apartments
- Manage booked apartments
- Manage sold apartments
- Add apartment prices
- Upload project and legal documents
- Submit projects for verification
- View verification status
- Receive buyer enquiries
- Manage enquiries related to their own projects
- View analytics for their own projects
- Manage their Builder profile

The Builder should be able to manage the following hierarchy:

BUILDER
↓
APARTMENT PROJECT
↓
TOWERS / BUILDINGS
↓
APARTMENTS / UNITS
↓
AVAILABILITY AND STATUS

Example statuses:

- Available
- Reserved
- Booked
- Sold

The Builder must NOT be able to:

- Access the Agent Dashboard
- Manage Agent clients
- Manage Agent leads
- Manage unrelated Agent listings
- Manage all properties on the SAI platform
- Manage all users on the platform
- Access platform-wide administration
- Access the Super Admin Control Panel

The Builder navigation should contain only:

- Builder Overview
- My Apartment Projects
- My Properties / Units
- Add Apartment Project
- Towers / Buildings
- Availability & Inventory
- Buyer Enquiries
- Analytics
- Verification & Documents
- Messages
- Builder Profile

==================================================
CRITICAL DIFFERENCE BETWEEN AGENT AND BUILDER
==================================================

AGENT:

The Agent generally manages individual property listings on behalf of owners or sellers.

Example:

"2BHK Apartment for Sale in Pune"

The Agent manages the listing, buyer enquiries, and clients.

BUILDER:

The Builder constructs an apartment project and manages multiple apartments or units within that project.

Example:

"Green Valley Apartments"

↓ Tower A

↓ Flat 101

↓ Flat 102

↓ Flat 103

Do not combine these two experiences.

An Agent should not see Builder project management.

A Builder should not see Agent client-management tools.

==================================================
ROLE SEPARATION RULES
==================================================

BUYER:

Can search, view, save, compare, and enquire about properties.

Cannot create or manage listings.

AGENT:

Can create and manage their own individual property listings, leads, and clients.

Cannot manage apartment construction projects.

BUILDER:

Can create and manage their own apartment construction projects, buildings, towers, apartments, units, and availability.

Cannot manage Agent clients or Agent-specific tools.

